00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:11.200
<v SPEAKER_00>You know, this took me a couple of years to put together.

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:12.799
<v SPEAKER_00>I did a bunch of research.

00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:18.560
<v SPEAKER_00>I visited a bunch of spots around the world to learn more about the impacts these data centers are having.

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:33.840
<v SPEAKER_00>And ultimately, not I don't just dig into the demands of these data centers, how they're affecting people, but what this means for our future, what the tech industry is actually trying to do by pushing all these data centers on us and whether we can do something different.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:39.200
<v SPEAKER_00>So I'm not sure if you're aware of this, but pre-orders are really important for new books.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:52.000
<v SPEAKER_00>It's not just like helping to sell books ahead of time, but it actually sends the signal to booksellers that this is a book that readers are interested in, that people are buying, and that more people will probably want to buy.

00:01:52.159 --> 00:02:02.879
